# Communication app status

Updated: 2026-11-14

## Implemented

- Session-based guest identities; no account or user-module changes are needed.
- Guest users can create private two-person chats, share an invite link and send an opening message.
- A second guest can join from the invite link; only the two participants can view or send messages.
- HTTP polling, unread counts, visible read receipts and sender-only soft deletion.
- Reservation conversations still use `open_conversation()`, `close_conversation()` and `mark_trip_completed()`.
- Twenty-four-hour expiry for trip conversations and the `close_conversations` command.
- Reviews limited to completed trips and their participants; one review per reviewer/target/trip.
- Rating summaries hidden until three reviews, staff review moderation and CSV export.
- Whole-word moderation with basic accent, repetition and character-substitution normalization.
- Responsive Blackberry/CoRide branding and communication-specific tests.

## Configuration and integration limits

- Guest access is enabled by default. Set Django's `COMMUNICATION_GUEST_MODE = False` or set `CORIDE_COMMUNICATION_GUEST_MODE=false` to require authenticated users. Existing guest sessions stop working while the flag is off.
- Guest identities are tied to the Django browser session. They are temporary and are not automatically merged with accounts when the user module is integrated.
- Reservations and trips still have no models or hooks in this branch. Reservation acceptance must call `open_conversation()` and trip completion must call `mark_trip_completed()`.
- Django Channels and Redis are not configured. Chat uses one-second HTTP polling; delivery is not guaranteed under one second as it would be with WebSockets.
- Configure `COMMUNICATION_BLOCKED_TERMS` in Django settings or `CORIDE_BLOCKED_TERMS` in the environment. No moderation vocabulary is bundled, and an ML classifier is not implemented.
- Only CSV review export is available; PDF and Excel require additional dependencies.

## Checks

```powershell
uv run manage.py check
uv run manage.py test communication
uv run manage.py makemigrations --check --dry-run
```
